  "chapter": 728,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 75 Chapter 728\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 5300, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  tax  law,  in relation to research tobacco\n        products\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would exempt medical research tobacco products from tax  and\nregulatory requirements intended for commercial tobacco products.\n \n  I  fully support the intent of this bill to exempt New York's research\ninstitutions from being subjected to taxes imposed on commercial  tobac-\nco,  when  such  tobacco  products are being utilized solely for medical\nresearch. As  originally  drafted,  technical  changes  were  needed  to\nprevent  fraud  and to ensure that untaxed tobacco products would not be\ndistributed to customers.\n\n  The Executive has secured an agreement with the  Legislature  to  pass\nlegislation  in the upcoming session to make these technical changes. On\nthis basis, I am signing this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2019
